{"name":"Lime It or Leave It","hex":"#8ca94a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lime","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any inorganic material containing calcium, usually calcium oxide (quicklime) or calcium hydroxide (slaked lime).","Any gluey or adhesive substance that traps or captures; sometimes a synonym for birdlime."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To treat with calcium hydroxide or calcium oxide (lime).","To smear with birdlime.\n To ensnare, catch, entrap."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lime"},{"term":"leave","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have a consequence or remnant.\n To cause or allow (something) to remain as available; to refrain from taking (something) away; to stop short of consuming or otherwise depleting (something) entirely.","To cause or allow (something) to remain as available; to refrain from taking (something) away; to stop short of consuming or otherwise depleting (something) entirely."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The action of the batsman not attempting to play at the ball.","The arrangement of balls in play that remains after a shot is made (which determines whether the next shooter — who may be either the same player, or an opponent — has good options, or only poor ones)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leave"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lime (transportation company)","blocks":[{"text":"Neutron Holdings, Inc., doing business under the name Lime, formerly LimeBike, is an American transportation company based in San Francisco, California. It runs electric scooters, electric bikes, and electric mopeds in more than 200 cities in nearly 30 countries around the world. The system offers dockless vehicles that users find and unlock via a smartphone app that knows the location of available vehicles via GPS."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Lime_Logos-wiki-01.svg/330px-Lime_Logos-wiki-01.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lime_(transportation_company)","wikidata":"Q39086685"},{"title":"Leave It","blocks":[{"text":"\"Leave It\" is a song by English rock band Yes. It appears on their 1983 album, 90125, and released as its second single, following \"Owner of a Lonely Heart\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5a/Yes_-_Leave_It.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leave_It","wikidata":"Q587771"},{"title":"Lime (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lime is a color that is a shade of yellow-green, so named because it is a representation of the color of the citrus fruit lime. It is the color that is in between the web color chartreuse and yellow on the color wheel. Alternate names for this color included yellow-green, lemon-lime, lime green, or bitter lime."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/AosaHGkyuai_%28cropped%29_3.jpg/330px-AosaHGkyuai_%28cropped%29_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lime_(color)","wikidata":"Q906936"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Lime_Scooter_4.1.jpg/500px-Lime_Scooter_4.1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Lime_Scooter_4.1.jpg/1280px-Lime_Scooter_4.1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Lime_Scooter_4.1.jpg/500px-Lime_Scooter_4.1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALime_Scooter_4.1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/A_Lime_e-bike_parked_on_a_paved_surface_in_Rochester_Riverside_-_Rochester%2C_Medway.jpg/250p